    "content": "Cameron and Cayden Boozer are elite fraternal twin basketball players committed to Duke (class of 2025), following their father, former NBA All-Star Carlos Boozer. As five-star recruits from Miami, they are known for dominating high school basketball and leading the USA Basketball U17 team to gold. Key Details About the Boozer Twins: Cameron Boozer (Forward): A 6'9\" power forward who excels in scoring, rebounding, and playmaking, often recognized as a premier national prospect. Cayden Boozer (Point Guard): A 6'3\" powerhouse point guard recognized for his high basketball IQ, passing ability, and ability to run the offense. Family Legacy: They are the sons of former Blue Devil and NBA player Carlos Boozer, who was a two-time All-Star. Recruitment: They committed to Duke in October 2024 over schools like Miami, Kentucky, and Florida. Background: The twins are from Miami, Florida, and played for Christopher Columbus High School. Both brothers are highly regarded for their combined skill sets, bringing a mix of size and guard play to the next level.",
